1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:05,550
Tsubasa and Misaki's combined twin header.

2
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:10,630
In the 25th minute of the first half, ties the score at 1-1.

3
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:14,430
Japan found the goal through teamwork.

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,390
Equalizer!

5
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:19,430
You didn't take them seriously enough, Müller.

6
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:24,440
You thought you could easily catch that vibrating shot.

7
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:27,440
And they exploited that weakness.

8
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:29,990
Actually, that wasn't a shot, it was a pass.

9
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:32,740
It was good that you saw it and stopped it.

10
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:37,410
But in the end, you missed it because of a slight mental weakness.

11
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:41,660
Number 10 comes to help from behind.

12
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:44,670
You still have a long way to go, Müller.

13
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:48,880
Your confidence is good, but if you underestimate your opponent...

14
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:51,010
...things like this happen.

15
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:07,320
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

16
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:26,710
The German youth were championship contenders, but Germany is fighting a tough battle against Japan.

17
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:29,130
They've equalized!

18
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:32,470
Mrs. Ozora! Tsubasa really did it!

19
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:35,390
Hooray! Tsubasa-senpai did it.

20
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,470
Yes.

21
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,480
Tsubasa.

22
00:02:38,810 --> 00:02:39,850
Well done, Misaki!

23
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:44,650
With this 1-1 equalizer, our players are even more motivated for the competition.

24
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:46,480
Thank you, Japan.

25
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:51,490
This feels better for us, who have been defeated by you.

26
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:54,950
Keep playing like this until the end!

27
00:02:55,830 --> 00:02:58,250
And the game restarts.

28
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:02,500
The midfield battle heats up again, and Ozora Tsubasa gets the ball.

29
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,750
Alright, let's go forward, guys.

30
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,380
With Tsubasa in midfield...

31
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:13,180
...as the backbone of the team, he doesn't let Germany hold and control the ball.

32
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,930
Tsubasa.

33
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:21,850
To win, you must become friends with the soccer ball.

34
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,610
How do we do that?

35
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,070
Always stay with it.

36
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:29,940
At school, while eating...

37
00:03:30,030 --> 00:03:32,780
...wherever you go, whatever you do, your ball should always be with you.

38
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,530
Morisaki!

39
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,490
The ball is your friend, so don't be afraid.

40
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:38,490
What?

41
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:41,080
So the ball is your friend?

42
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:44,250
Then catch your friend!

43
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:47,000
- Tsubasa, watch out!
- Tsubasa!

44
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:50,010
Oh! The ball hits him in the face.

45
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,680
See, no problem.

46
00:03:55,470 --> 00:03:56,510
Tsubasa.

47
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:01,230
Okay.

48
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:04,230
I understand, Tsubasa.

49
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:08,150
I'm not afraid anymore. I'll do it.

50
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,030
The ball is your friend.

51
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:15,370
He still carries what I said that day in his heart.

52
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,990
He strikes the ball directly!

53
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:22,500
Tsubasa rushes in and the ball hits him right in the face!

54
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:27,630
I'm fine. I'm fine. The ball is always my friend.

55
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:33,260
Tsubasa always goes beyond what I teach.

56
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,640
It was like that then too...

57
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:47,060
What?

58
00:04:54,610 --> 00:04:55,910
It's a goal!

59
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:57,280
Great.

60
00:04:57,370 --> 00:04:59,410
Wh- What coolness!

61
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,500
What do you say? Will you coach me?

62
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:04,410
Yes, of course.

63
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:05,920
Alright.

64
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,920
Tsubasa.

65
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:14,260
Impossible!

66
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,680
What? Hey!

67
00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:25,440
Tsubasa!

68
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:27,850
Are you okay?

69
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:30,480
It's very difficult.

70
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:33,940
Tsubasa does a cartwheel and flip.

71
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:35,900
And then another flip!

72
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:40,410
He takes the opponent's skill and makes it his own.

73
00:05:40,530 --> 00:05:42,450
This is Tsubasa's talent!

74
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,790
Become a midfielder.

75
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:49,130
These two can truly organize Japan's game.

76
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,340
Drive Shot.

77
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:54,340
This is how South America's long-distance shot is.

78
00:05:58,550 --> 00:06:03,390
Tsubasa has completely learned everything you wrote for him in the notebook.

79
00:06:05,390 --> 00:06:06,520
Please.

80
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:11,520
Tsubasa wants to go to Brazil and hopes you'll be his coach, Roberto-san.

81
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:15,990
This time, make Tsubasa's dream come true.

82
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:23,370
I broke my promise and returned from Japan to Brazil without you.

83
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,120
And still...

84
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:28,580
...you didn't give up on me.

85
00:06:28,870 --> 00:06:33,750
Tsubasa gets the ball again, but the Germans resist.

86
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:37,050
You followed my trainings.

87
00:06:38,130 --> 00:06:40,130
You've progressed a lot.

88
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:44,180
Roberto-san, I finally found you.

89
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:45,390
You...

90
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:52,230
Have you thought more about taking Tsubasa to Brazil?

91
00:06:53,310 --> 00:06:54,150
Yes.

92
00:06:54,570 --> 00:06:58,610
But I'm not the only one who wants to take him.

93
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,530
What?

94
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:03,240
This is Barbas, the coach of the Argentina youth team.

95
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,530
Pleased to meet you.

96
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:07,370
So you want to take Tsubasa to Argentina?

97
00:07:07,450 --> 00:07:12,290
Yes, I want to talk to him as soon as the tournament ends.

98
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:16,420
But we made a bet.

99
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,960
A bet?

100
00:07:18,050 --> 00:07:22,800
If Japan loses, I take him; if Japan wins, Roberto takes him.

101
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:28,310
If Japan wins, Roberto-san, will you really take Tsubasa to Brazil?

102
00:07:29,270 --> 00:07:30,100
Yes.

103
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:32,980
Thank you!

104
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:37,400
Sorry, Coach Barbas, but Japan will win.

105
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,320
What?

106
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:42,070
Japan... will win.

107
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,450
This way, Takeshi.

108
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:44,660
Get the ball.

109
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,410
The midfield battle continues.

110
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:51,000
Japan is on the quest to conquer the world.

111
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:55,210
And their generation is bringing a rebirth for Japanese football.

112
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:59,300
This new generation wants to be the best in the world.

113
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:02,470
The legend begins with victory in this tournament.

114
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,010
Katagiri-san.

115
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:11,350
The first half's time is about to expire.

116
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:15,100
So will it end 1-1?

117
00:08:15,730 --> 00:08:17,900
Oh, the ball is loose.

118
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:20,110
The ball falls between them.

119
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:21,190
I'll get it.

120
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:22,400
Never!

121
00:08:22,490 --> 00:08:25,570
Will Sano or Max reach it first?

122
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:29,160
Schneider, I'm getting it!

123
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:33,540
Once again, Schneider gets the ball in midfield.

124
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:36,250
He starts dribbling toward Japan's goal.

125
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:38,040
- Don't let him pass!
- Okay!

126
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:39,420
This is a battle!

127
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,010
Japan's defense confronts him!

128
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:45,510
It seems this is his last chance in the first half.

129
00:08:45,890 --> 00:08:46,760
Guys!

130
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,010
Karl!

131
00:08:51,810 --> 00:08:55,270
Schneider's moves are unique! He passed two players at once.

132
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:58,480
Schneider is always calm and composed.

133
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:01,780
But this equalizer has angered him.

134
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,360
I can feel it.

135
00:09:04,530 --> 00:09:08,990
His fighting spirit burns with blue flames.

136
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:11,540
Come on, Schneider!

137
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,210
Score if you can!

138
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:15,790
Wakabayashi.

139
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,710
Don't let him reach Wakabayashi!

140
00:09:18,790 --> 00:09:20,210
We'll stop him!

141
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:23,050
Oh, Schneider passes.

142
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,590
What?

143
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:25,590
Schneider!

144
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:28,550
Kaltz comes in with a through pass.

145
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:29,640
Good.

146
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,600
No!

147
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:36,600
Extraordinary! Schneider passes through Japan's defense without being offside.

148
00:09:36,730 --> 00:09:39,860
The cunning Kaltz delivered a precise pass.

149
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,360
Wakabayashi leaves his goal without hesitation.

150
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:45,070
This is one-on-one with Schneider.

151
00:09:45,610 --> 00:09:46,610
Wakabayashi!

152
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:47,610
Wakabayashi!

153
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:48,870
Schneider!

154
00:09:49,870 --> 00:09:53,370
Schneider shoots directly!

155
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:01,250
Wakabayashi's hat is shattered!

156
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,210
The ball also hits the crossbar!

157
00:10:04,590 --> 00:10:07,050
And it bursts from the force! What!?

158
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:11,760
Schneider's Fire Shot was unfortunately not a goal!

159
00:10:13,390 --> 00:10:16,270
And the final whistle of the first half blows.

160
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,070
Wa- Wakabayashi!

161
00:10:22,150 --> 00:10:23,270
Wakabayashi!

162
00:10:23,570 --> 00:10:26,530
Oh, Wakabayashi is bleeding!

163
00:10:26,990 --> 00:10:32,280
It seems Schneider's shot hit Wakabayashi directly in the face.

164
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:38,290
Now Schneider's Fire Shot hit his face and he doesn't even blink.

165
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:40,790
Just what you'd expect from you, Wakabayashi.

166
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:42,540
Right, Schneider.

167
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:46,420
If you don't come back stronger in the second half...

168
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:50,220
...you'll never have a chance to beat us!

169
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,560
Okay. I'll put you in your place, Wakabayashi!

170
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:57,430
I'll score two goals against you in the second half.

171
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:02,940
I'll complete my hat-trick in every match of this tournament.

172
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,440
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

173
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,970
Born: January 9 | Height: 169 cm | Weight: 58 kg | Blood Type: A

174
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:17,640
The final between Japan and Germany is intense.

175
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:20,480
The first half ended in a 1-1 draw.

176
00:11:20,770 --> 00:11:22,890
The exchange of offense and defense is equal.

177
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:26,230
So far, Germany had won all its matches overwhelmingly.

178
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,940
This must be shocking for them.

179
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:31,320
- Damn it!
- Japan is great.

180
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:35,370
On the other hand, Japan has become stronger than before.

181
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:38,790
Being in the final proves that.

182
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:40,410
Well done, Japan!

183
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:41,910
You're doing a great job!

184
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,580
Keep it up in the second half too.

185
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:46,000
Our Japan youth team...

186
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:50,510
...has gotten even stronger in Europe in every match of the tournament.

187
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:52,670
Wakabayashi, you're bleeding.

188
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:54,630
Genzo, go get treatment.

189
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,470
- Yes, coach.
- This way.

190
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:57,390
Yes.

191
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:01,520
Do you know why you conceded that goal?

192
00:12:06,940 --> 00:12:08,150
Pride!

193
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:12,240
When you underestimate your opponent, things like this happen.

194
00:12:13,990 --> 00:12:15,780
Your confidence is good.

195
00:12:15,950 --> 00:12:20,910
But underestimating your opponent eventually turns into your weak point.

196
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:23,160
Do you understand, Müller?

197
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,080
Yes, coach!

198
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:28,290
Alright, now don't forget!

199
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:29,250
Yes, coach.

200
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:36,180
I wish I could go there and give advice to Tsubasa.

201
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,680
But...

202
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:39,970
Roberto-san.

203
00:12:40,850 --> 00:12:43,930
If you have a message for Tsubasa, I'll convey it to him.

204
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:52,440
Even the lion, the king of animals, uses all its strength to hunt a rabbit.

205
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,530
Don't forget this, Müller.

206
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:56,450
Yes, coach.

207
00:12:56,860 --> 00:13:00,070
If you follow this teaching, they won't be able to score against you again.

208
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,120
Yes, coach.

209
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:04,040
Alright, go back to your team.

210
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:04,950
Yes, coach.

211
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,080
Thank you very much.

212
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,000
Müller is still young.

213
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:15,210
He's still mentally soft.

214
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,470
In my notebook...

215
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:20,850
...there's something I noted on page 52.

216
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:24,220
Tell him not to forget it.

217
00:13:25,310 --> 00:13:28,140
Okay, page 52.

218
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,730
Wakabayashi.

219
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:30,690
Wakabayashi.

220
00:13:30,770 --> 00:13:31,810
Are you okay?

221
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,730
Yes.

222
00:13:33,230 --> 00:13:34,730
It's nothing serious.

223
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:39,280
The Fire Shot is very powerful.

224
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:43,240
Jito and I didn't even touch it, but we still got injured.

225
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:44,740
Right.

226
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:49,750
My injury is also from Schneider's Fire Shot.

227
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:53,040
I worked hard to get payback for it.

228
00:13:53,590 --> 00:13:56,260
But I had to sit on the bench before I could do it.

229
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:01,260
Wakabayashi, go out there in the second half for me.

230
00:14:01,510 --> 00:14:03,010
Wakashimazu.

231
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,430
Okay!

232
00:14:06,270 --> 00:14:09,310
I'll settle the score with him for you, Wakashimazu.

233
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:10,770
Yes! I trust you!

234
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,520
The defensive line...

235
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:15,610
did a good job in the first half.

236
00:14:15,690 --> 00:14:16,530
Mizugi!

237
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:19,530
Let's go into the second half with the same defensive setup.

238
00:14:20,070 --> 00:14:24,620
And in midfield, watch out for Kaltz.

239
00:14:25,370 --> 00:14:28,000
I think he has a trick up his sleeve.

240
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:29,540
I understand.

241
00:14:29,790 --> 00:14:31,250
30 minutes left in the second half.

242
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:34,500
Fight for us, for those watching from the bench.

243
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:36,500
- Okay!
- Leave it to us.

244
00:14:36,590 --> 00:14:37,510
Yes!

245
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:40,680
About our roles in the second half...

246
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,010
Hyuga-san!

247
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,510
What is it, Takeshi?

248
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,020
Is your leg okay?

249
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:51,520
It's fine. Trust me until the end, coach.

250
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:55,440
I am Japan's forward, and my goal is to become number 1 in the world.

251
00:14:55,820 --> 00:15:00,280
I won't let this match end without scoring a goal.

252
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:03,530
Okay.

253
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:05,990
Go and score for us.

254
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:06,910
Yes, coach.

255
00:15:06,990 --> 00:15:08,450
Hyuga-san, take this.

256
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,040
Thanks, Takeshi.

257
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:12,080
Are you better now?

258
00:15:12,170 --> 00:15:14,040
Sorry, senpais.

259
00:15:14,130 --> 00:15:15,540
What are you saying?

260
00:15:16,090 --> 00:15:19,800
This is the only thing we can do from the bench.

261
00:15:21,130 --> 00:15:25,510
But if you don't play well, we'll come and take your place without hesitation.

262
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:28,220
Go and score against them in the second half.

263
00:15:28,310 --> 00:15:29,140
Okay.

264
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:31,390
This is a good team.

265
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:32,850
I agree.

266
00:15:33,690 --> 00:15:37,860
Both those playing and those on the bench.

267
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:42,400
Everyone is striving for victory together.

268
00:15:42,490 --> 00:15:44,950
Takeshi, I trust your passes in the second half.

269
00:15:45,030 --> 00:15:46,870
The team is truly acting in unity.

270
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:48,030
Sorry.

271
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,540
Don't worry about it.

272
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,450
Go and play for us too.

273
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:54,420
There's no reason such a unique team can't win.

274
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,330
Isn't that right?

275
00:15:59,000 --> 00:15:59,840
Yes, coach.

276
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:03,590
This is the last 30 minutes.

277
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:08,100
After this, we'll say goodbye again, Tsubasa.

278
00:16:08,930 --> 00:16:10,100
Misaki.

279
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,640
I know I said the same thing last year.

280
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:17,360
Let's win this tournament first.

281
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:19,860
Okay!

282
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:23,070
We're doing well, Tsubasa.

283
00:16:25,570 --> 00:16:28,120
You're still letting them hold the ball too much in midfield.

284
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:31,290
Stop them quicker and send the ball to the attack line.

285
00:16:31,370 --> 00:16:33,040
Defense, your tackles aren't fast enough.

286
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:36,370
Don't let them reach the goal, break them up more upfront.

287
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,170
O- Okay, coach.

288
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:39,380
Sorry.

289
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:44,380
Don't be so harsh on them, coach.

290
00:16:44,510 --> 00:16:46,130
Schneider.

291
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:48,640
We're playing against a strong Japan.

292
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:54,270
Their skill and spirit are just like ours.

293
00:16:54,810 --> 00:16:55,640
But...

294
00:16:56,810 --> 00:16:59,020
Germany doesn't lose!

295
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:05,610
We, Germany, have been maintaining the championship tradition in European football since the past.

296
00:17:05,990 --> 00:17:11,080
Our history is long and full of glorious titles.

297
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:13,660
This history of German football...

298
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:17,670
...cannot be easily changed by Japan!

299
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,790
Isn't that right, guys?

300
00:17:20,170 --> 00:17:21,290
Yes!

301
00:17:22,050 --> 00:17:24,670
Schneider... guys.

302
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:27,430
Aren't you Mr. Schneider?

303
00:17:27,550 --> 00:17:28,380
What?

304
00:17:28,470 --> 00:17:30,300
The former coach of Hamburg.

305
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:31,970
Y- Yes.

306
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:33,470
I guessed correctly.

307
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:34,810
Hey, guys!

308
00:17:34,890 --> 00:17:36,520
Karl Heinz Schneider's family is here.

309
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:40,940
The one who scored Germany's first goal.

310
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,400
Will you give a speech?

311
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,700
Hooray!

312
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:50,110
Schneider is the best!

313
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:53,450
He is undoubtedly the one who brought Germany to this stage.

314
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:59,210
As long as your son Karl Heinz Schneider is here, we will definitely win!

315
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,300
Thank you, thank you.

316
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,510
Rudi.

317
00:18:09,050 --> 00:18:12,100
It seems Karl has become very famous.

318
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,010
Yes.

319
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:16,970
Right. I'm really proud of my big brother.

320
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:19,890
I'm going to get some juice, okay?

321
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:22,150
- Be careful.
- Okay!

322
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,740
Actually...

323
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:32,990
I've decided to go to Munich.

324
00:18:33,490 --> 00:18:35,660
You mean Karl's Munich?

325
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:37,040
Yes.

326
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:39,910
Coach Falster transferred Karl.

327
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,790
And he's giving me the opportunity to be an assistant coach too.

328
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:46,710
Really? That's great.

329
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:50,510
Thanks. Do you really think so?

330
00:18:51,050 --> 00:18:52,010
Yes.

331
00:18:56,350 --> 00:18:58,020
Well...

332
00:18:58,890 --> 00:19:03,230
Actually, I had come to your workplace...

333
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:06,570
...to invite you to Karl's last match in Hamburg.

334
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:10,450
So the man with you then...

335
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:12,780
I mean... that...

336
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,410
What are you saying!

337
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,790
He is one of the managers at my workplace.

338
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:24,420
We had just gone out for lunch with the others.

339
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:28,050
S- So that's what it was.

340
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:30,760
Because of you, Rudi.

341
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:33,510
Dad, Mom!

342
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:35,550
Here, drinks.

343
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:37,850
Thank you, Marie.

344
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:39,970
I bought one for you too, Mom.

345
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:41,890
Thank you, Marie.

346
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:44,690
Delicious.

347
00:19:44,770 --> 00:19:45,810
Yes.

348
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:48,320
Which flavor did you get, Marie?

349
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,280
I got a delicious one.

350
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:52,570
Misaki's father.

351
00:19:53,110 --> 00:19:55,660
Misaki is really a wonderful player.

352
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:57,780
Thank you.

353
00:19:57,910 --> 00:20:00,160
Misaki, when this match is over...

354
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,500
...he said he would say goodbye to everyone.

355
00:20:04,790 --> 00:20:08,090
That's why he will do his best not to have any regrets.

356
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:10,960
Taro.

357
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:15,090
Because of my painting work...

358
00:20:15,180 --> 00:20:18,810
...you didn't join any club in France.

359
00:20:19,310 --> 00:20:22,140
You reunited with your best friend.

360
00:20:22,390 --> 00:20:28,020
And now you're playing with all your strength against the world again, with no regrets.

361
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:34,530
Taro, I've finally made my final decision.

362
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:37,950
I'd rather try than live with the regret of not doing it.

363
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,330
Isn't that right?

364
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:41,950
It's time.

365
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,160
Alright, let's go.

366
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:47,920
For the honor of German football, let's bring the championship cup home!

367
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:49,420
Okay!

368
00:20:50,170 --> 00:20:52,920
You've come this far, there's not much to say.

369
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:56,720
The only thing I can say is use all your strength.

370
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,640
And fight in the second half.

371
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,850
Yes, coach.

372
00:21:00,430 --> 00:21:02,430
Are you ready, guys?

373
00:21:02,810 --> 00:21:04,180
Yes!

374
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:06,230
Alright, let's go!

375
00:21:06,310 --> 00:21:07,520
Yes!

376
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:13,690
Roberto returned to Brazil, but they're showing the match there too.

377
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:15,450
I'm sure he's watching!

378
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,610
We'll definitely win, Roberto.

379
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,700
I will win.

380
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:26,290
And I'll go to Brazil, the football country where Roberto is waiting.

381
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:28,290
Tsubasa!

382
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:32,090
Katagiri-san.

383
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:34,340
Page 52 of the notebook.

384
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:35,590
What?

385
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,220
Page 52 of the notebook?

386
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:40,600
Hey, Tsubasa.

387
00:21:40,930 --> 00:21:45,100
Hurry up. We can't start without you.

388
00:21:45,390 --> 00:21:46,310
Okay.

389
00:21:49,650 --> 00:21:52,110
Notebook... Notebook?

390
00:21:52,650 --> 00:21:54,190
Notebook, you mean...

391
00:21:55,820 --> 00:21:56,900
Notebook!

392
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:58,200
Roberto!?

393
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:01,530
Th- This is impossible!

394
00:22:02,410 --> 00:22:03,620
Roberto...

395
00:23:46,710 --> 00:23:49,980
Next Episode: Reply to the Message